<title>POLAND: Poland C/A deficit up to $2.41 bln in Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Poland C/A deficit up to $2.41 bln in Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland had a current account deficit of $135 million in May bringing the shortfall in the January-May period to $2.41 billion, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p> POLISH CURRENT ACCOUNT	  MAY 1997     APRIL 97    MAY  96</p>
<p> current account mln USD	    -135	    -742	  -14</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	  -824	    -935	 -649</p>
<p> exports				 2,035	   2,361	2,030</p>
<p> imports				 2,859	   3,296	2,679</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	  552	     536	  574</p>
<p>					 JAN-MAY 1997  JAN-MAY 1996</p>
<p> current account mln USD	  -2,410	    -207</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	-4,826	  -2,611</p>
<p> exports				10,162	   9,535</p>
<p> imports				14,988	  12,146</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	2,304	   3,023</p>
<p>Note. Revised figures in brackets. From January 1996 the central bank introduced a new category, &quot;unclassified flows&quot; which encompasses mainly unregistered cross-border trade flows.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
